.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command is deprecated.
It is used to maintain an SRP (secure remote password) file.
At most one of the
.Sy -add ,
.Sy -modify ,
.Sy -delete ,
and
.Sy -list
options can be specified.
These options take zero or more usernames as parameters and perform the
appropriate operation on the SRP file.
For
.Sy -list ,
if no
.Em user
is given then all users are displayed.
.Pp
The configuration file to use, and the section within the file, can be
specified with the
.Sy -config
and
.Sy -name
flags, respectively.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy -help
Display an option summary.
.It Sy -verbose
Generate verbose output while processing.
.It Sy -add
Add a user and SRP verifier.
.It Sy -modify
Modify the SRP verifier of an existing user.
.It Sy -delete
Delete user from verifier file.
.It Sy -list
List users.
.It Sy -name
The particular SRP definition to use.
.It Sy -srpvfile Em file
If the config file is not specified,
.Sy -srpvfile
can be used to specify the file to operate on.
.It Sy -gn
Specifies the
.Sy g
and
.Sy N
values, using one of the strengths defined in IETF RFC 5054.
.It Sy -userinfo
specifies additional information to add when adding or modifying a user.
.It Sy -passin Em arg Ns , Sy -passout Em arg
The password source for the input and output file.
For more information about the format of
.Sy arg
see
.Xr openssl-passphrase-options 1 .
.It Sy -engine Em id
See
.Xr openssl 1 .
This option is deprecated.
.It Sy -rand Em files Ns , Sy -writerand Em file
See
.Xr openssl 1
for details.
.It Sy -provider Em name
.It Sy -provider-path Em path
.It Sy -provparam Em [name:]key=value
.It Sy -propquery Em propq
See
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
and
.Xr property 7 .
.It Sy -config Em configfile
See
.Xr openssl 1 .
.Pp
.Pf [ Sy -rand
.Em files ]
.Pf [ Sy -writerand
.Em file ]
.El
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Sy -engine
option was deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
